Guard the RockEnums.h include under MIGRAPHX_MLIR

mlir.cpp is compiled unconditionally (it provides the stub path when the
MLIR backend is disabled), but the <mlir-c/Dialect/RockEnums.h> include
sits ABOVE the #ifdef MIGRAPHX_MLIR block — so a build with
MIGRAPHX_ENABLE_MLIR=OFF (no rocMLIR present) dies on the include even
though every RockEnums consumer in the file is correctly guarded (the
tuning-table handles and mlirRockTuning* calls all live inside the
MIGRAPHX_MLIR region; migraphx/gpu/mlir.hpp references no Rock symbol).
Move the include beside its sibling <mlir-c/Dialect/Rock.h> inside the
guard — upstream intent unambiguous, same class as the rocsolver rfinfo
guard slip.

--- a/src/targets/gpu/mlir.cpp
+++ b/src/targets/gpu/mlir.cpp
@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@
 #include <migraphx/dead_code_elimination.hpp>
 #include <migraphx/pass_manager.hpp>
 #include <migraphx/gpu/mlir.hpp>
-#include <mlir-c/Dialect/RockEnums.h>
 #include <numeric>
 #include <ostream>
 
@@ -39,6 +38,7 @@
 #include <mlir-c/IR.h>
 #include <mlir-c/BuiltinAttributes.h>
 #include <mlir-c/BuiltinTypes.h>
+#include <mlir-c/Dialect/RockEnums.h>
 #include <mlir-c/Diagnostics.h>
 #include <mlir-c/Dialect/MIGraphX.h>
 #include <mlir-c/Dialect/Rock.h>
